   "evidence": "`def trajectorySection (V : F \u2192 F) (\u03b3 : \u211d \u2192 F) (hV : LipschitzWith K V) ...` with `K` coming from the section `variable {K : \u211d\u22650}`. In the body, `K` only enters through the proof `memLp_comp_add_toZeroAtInfty_sub hp hV h\u03b3 \u03be`, and `toLp` does not depend on that proof.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/ODE/TrajectoryOperator/Section.lean",
   "fix": "Remove `K` from the definition's signature, e.g. take `hV : \u2203 K, LipschitzWith K V`. Alternatively, add a lemma `trajectorySection_congr` (marked `@[simp]` if it normalizes) stating that the section is independent of the Lipschitz witness.",
   "issue": "`trajectorySection V \u03b3 hV h\u03b3 hp` depends on the implicit data `K` from `hV : LipschitzWith K V`, which nothing in its value uses. Two sections of the same field built from different constants (for example `hK.neg` against some other Lipschitz proof of `-\u2207f`) are different terms. The body is not exposed, so a consumer cannot prove them equal by `rfl` and there is no congruence lemma to use instead.",
